IMPORT prelude

-- Control of Essential Supplies Act 1973 (Singapore) -- what the Act asks of a person or business dealing in an article the President
-- has declared "controlled" or "rationed": licences and the appeal against the Controller (s 7), the trading offences (ss 14 to 19),
-- storage away from licensed premises and unclaimed seized goods (s 20), unlawful possession (s 21), penalties and the liability of
-- directors, partners and employers (s 22), the owner's payment when the Controller takes the goods (s 11(2)(b)), and composition (s 29).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CESA1973.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The last amendment
-- its Legislative History annotates is Act 15 of 2010 (Criminal Procedure Code 2010, s 430 and item 26 of the Sixth Schedule, in force
-- 2 January 2011). The deposit's metadata records it as the current version at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0096 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the provisions a trader or a member of the public meets. Not encoded: appointment of officers (ss 3, 4), the
-- regulation-making power (s 6) except as the source of s 14's quantity limits, the Controller's information, entry, arrest and
-- seizure powers (ss 8 to 10) beyond noting that obstruction is an offence, sale of perishable seized goods (s 12), delegation (ss 13,
-- 24), the court's confiscation power (s 26), protection of informers (s 30), and every order and regulation made under the Act. No President's order under s 5 was
-- retrieved, so this row cannot say which articles, if any, are controlled today.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions as shown in the finished example rows. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Control of Essential Supplies Act 1973 -- offences`

§§ `5 and 2 -- the Act bites only on a declared article`

-- s 5: "The President may, by order in the Gazette, declare any article or food to be a controlled article or to be a rationed article
-- or both." s 2: "controlled article" means an article or food declared under s 5, "and includes a rationed article"; "sell" includes
-- "barter or exchange".
GIVEN `declared controlled` IS A BOOLEAN, `declared rationed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the article is a controlled article` IF
    `declared controlled` OR `declared rationed`

§§ `7 -- licences, and the appeal to the Minister`

-- s 7(5): the Controller "may at any time, without assigning any reason for doing so, vary the conditions of or suspend or revoke or
-- refuse to renew any licence or permit". s 7(6): "Any person aggrieved by the Controller's refusal to issue or renew a licence under
-- this section or by any action of the Controller under subsection (5) may appeal against the refusal or action to the Minister whose
-- decision is final."
--
-- Read literally, a refusal to ISSUE a PERMIT is in neither limb: (6) names only a licence for refusal to issue, and (5) covers refusal
-- to renew, not refusal to issue. That gap is a reading of the words, not something the Act says outright.
DECLARE `Controller's decision` IS ONE OF
    `refusal to issue a licence`
    `refusal to renew a licence`
    `refusal to issue a permit`
    `refusal to renew a permit`
    `variation of conditions`
    `suspension`
    `revocation`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Controller's decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision can be appealed to the Minister` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `refusal to issue a permit` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 7(4): a person required to hold a licence or permit "must, on demand, produce" it to the Controller, an officer of customs or an
-- authorised person, "and any person who fails to do so shall be guilty of an offence".
GIVEN `licence required` IS A BOOLEAN, `demand made` IS A BOOLEAN, `produced it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to produce the licence is an offence` IF
    `licence required` AND `demand made` AND (NOT `produced it`)

§§ `16 -- selling without, or outside, a licence`

-- s 16(1): a person "not being the holder of a valid licence or permit issued in accordance with section 7, who sells by wholesale or
-- retail any controlled article -- (a) on the person's own behalf; (b) on behalf of any body corporate of which the person is a director
-- or an officer; or (c) on behalf of any firm of which the person is a partner" commits an offence. (2): a holder who sells "(a) in any
-- premises or at a place other than the premises or place specified in the licence or permit; or (b) contrary to any conditions
-- expressed in the licence or permit".
--
-- An employee selling for an employer, who is not a director, officer or partner, is outside s 16(1)(a) to (c) on its words; the
-- employer may still answer for the employee under s 22(5). That is a reading, labelled as such in NOTES.md.
DECLARE `Selling capacity` IS ONE OF
    `on own behalf`
    `for a company as director or officer`
    `for a firm as partner`
    `as an employee only`

GIVEN `capacity` IS A `Selling capacity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the capacity is within s 16(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `capacity`
    WHEN `as an employee only` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `sold a controlled article` IS A BOOLEAN, `capacity` IS A `Selling capacity`, `holds a valid licence or permit` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `at the licensed place` IS A BOOLEAN, `within the licence conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sale is an offence under s 16` IF
    `sold a controlled article`
    AND (    ((NOT `holds a valid licence or permit`) AND `the capacity is within s 16(1)` `capacity`)
         OR  (`holds a valid licence or permit` AND ((NOT `at the licensed place`) OR (NOT `within the licence conditions`))))

§§ `14, 15 -- over-quota sales, hoarding and refusing to supply`

-- s 14: selling a controlled article to another person "in excess of the quantity which may be lawfully acquired by such other person in
-- accordance with any regulations made under section 6" is an offence. s 15: a person "who conceals or destroys any controlled article
-- in order to withhold the article from the market or refuses, without reasonable cause, to supply any controlled article" commits an
-- offence.
GIVEN `quantity sold` IS A NUMBER, `buyer's lawful limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sale exceeds the buyer's quota` IF
    `quantity sold` GREATER THAN `buyer's lawful limit`

GIVEN `concealed or destroyed to withhold from the market` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused to supply` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `withholding is an offence under s 15` IF
        `concealed or destroyed to withhold from the market`
    OR  (`refused to supply` AND (NOT `had reasonable cause`))

§§ `17, 18 -- display, and rationed articles`

-- s 17(1): a person carrying on retail business at licensed premises "must display in a conspicuous position -- (a) the original of the
-- licence; and (b) a list in the English language and in any other language as the Controller may direct of the controlled articles or
-- rationed articles sold". (2): failure is an offence.
GIVEN `retail at licensed premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `original licence displayed` IS A BOOLEAN, `English list displayed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the display duty is broken` IF
    `retail at licensed premises` AND ((NOT `original licence displayed`) OR (NOT `English list displayed`))

-- s 18(1): "Except under the authority of the Controller or under and in accordance with this Act or of any direction, licence, permit or
-- coupon issued thereunder, a person must not obtain or attempt to obtain, and a retailer must not supply or offer or attempt to supply,
-- any rationed article." The buyer, not only the seller, commits the offence.
GIVEN `obtained or tried to obtain a rationed article` IS A BOOLEAN, `had authority or a coupon` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `obtaining the rationed article is an offence` IF
    `obtained or tried to obtain a rationed article` AND (NOT `had authority or a coupon`)

§§ `19 -- conditions a seller may impose`

-- s 19: a person who, in selling a controlled article, "imposes, except with the Controller's permission, any condition of sale other
-- than a condition of sale -- (a) requiring immediate payment for the controlled article; (b) prescribing the time within which payment
-- must be made or delivery taken; or (c) requiring a deposit" commits an offence. So tying (buy X to get Y) is an offence unless
-- permitted.
DECLARE `Condition of sale` IS ONE OF
    `immediate payment`
    `time for payment or delivery`
    `a deposit`
    `buying another product too`
    `a minimum purchase`
    `membership of a club`

GIVEN `the condition` IS A `Condition of sale`, `Controller permitted it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the condition is lawful` IF
        `Controller permitted it`
    OR  CONSIDER `the condition`
        WHEN `immediate payment` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `time for payment or delivery` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a deposit` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `20 -- storage away from licensed premises, and unclaimed goods`

-- s 20(1): removing a controlled article from licensed premises, or storing it "in any premises, other than licensed premises or
-- premises approved by the Controller for such storage", is an offence. (3): proof that the defendant's article "was found in premises
-- other than licensed premises or premises approved by the Controller" is sufficient, "and the burden of proving that the defendant is
-- not guilty ... then lies upon the defendant". (4): an article removed in a search, "if not claimed within 2 weeks of the removal, may
-- be sold by order of the Controller, and the proceeds of the sale must be paid into the Consolidated Fund".
GIVEN `stored away from licensed premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `premises approved by the Controller` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `defendant proved innocence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the storage is an offence under s 20` IF
    `stored away from licensed premises` AND (NOT `premises approved by the Controller`) AND (NOT `defendant proved innocence`)

-- "within 2 weeks" is read as 14 days: a sale may be ordered from day 15 if no claim has been made. The day count is an inference; the
-- text does not say how the fortnight is reckoned.
GIVEN `days since removal` IS A NUMBER, `claimed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Controller may order the unclaimed article sold` IF
    (NOT `claimed`) AND `days since removal` GREATER THAN 14

§§ `21 -- unlawful possession`

-- s 21: possession or control of a controlled article "in such circumstances as to raise a reasonable suspicion that an offence under
-- this Act has been or is intended to be committed" is an offence "unless he or she satisfies the court that the offence has not been
-- and was not intended to be committed by him or her".
GIVEN `reasonable suspicion` IS A BOOLEAN, `satisfied the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the possession is an offence under s 21` IF
    `reasonable suspicion` AND (NOT `satisfied the court`)

§§ `11(2)(b) -- payment when the Controller takes the goods`

-- s 11(2)(b): where a maximum price is fixed by written law, the Controller "may pay to the owner of the controlled article the price so
-- fixed less an amount not exceeding 25% of the price being the expenses certified by the Controller to have been incurred" in taking
-- possession, storing and restoring possession.
GIVEN `fixed price` IS A NUMBER, `certified expenses` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction allowed` MEANS
    IF `certified expenses` GREATER THAN `fixed price` TIMES 25 DIVIDED BY 100
    THEN `fixed price` TIMES 25 DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE `certified expenses`

GIVEN `fixed price` IS A NUMBER, `certified expenses` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payment to the owner` MEANS
    `fixed price` MINUS `the deduction allowed` `fixed price` `certified expenses`

§§ `22 -- penalties`

-- s 22(1): a person other than a body corporate, "but including a director or an officer of a body corporate", is liable "to a fine not
-- exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both and, in the case of a second or subsequent
-- conviction, to a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both". (2): "Any body corporate
-- which commits an offence under this Act shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000."
--
-- A repeat conviction doubles the fine but not the prison term, and a body corporate pays the same $20,000 on a first or a tenth
-- conviction.
GIVEN `is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `is a body corporate` THEN 20000
    ELSE IF `is a repeat conviction` THEN 20000
         ELSE 10000

GIVEN `is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum prison term in years` MEANS
    IF `is a body corporate` THEN 0
    ELSE 2

-- s 22(4)(b): where a body corporate is convicted, every director or officer at the time "shall be deemed to be guilty of the offence
-- unless he or she proves that the offence was committed without his or her knowledge or that he or she took reasonable precautions to
-- prevent its commission".
GIVEN `company convicted` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved lack of knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the director is deemed guilty` IF
    `company convicted` AND (NOT `proved lack of knowledge`) AND (NOT `proved reasonable precautions`)

-- s 22(5): a person is liable to the same penalty for a thing done or omitted "by his or her partner, agent or employee, unless he or she
-- proves that he or she took reasonable precautions to prevent the doing or omission of that thing".
GIVEN `done by partner, agent or employee` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal is liable` IF
    `done by partner, agent or employee` AND (NOT `proved reasonable precautions`)

-- s 22(3): on conviction the court may, "whether or not it imposes any other penalty", cancel the licence and debar the person, firm or
-- corporation "either absolutely or for a period", or suspend the licence. Not computed: it is a discretion.

§§ `29 -- composition`

-- s 29(1): the Controller "may compound any offence under this Act prescribed as being an offence which may be compounded by collecting
-- from the person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum of money not exceeding $2,000". No regulations under
-- s 29(2) prescribing compoundable offences were retrieved.
GIVEN `offence prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition is within s 29` IF
    `offence prescribed as compoundable` AND `sum` AT MOST 2000
